cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ClawSec in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ClawSec: encrypted netcat with a password-authenticated key exchange"
abstract: >-
  ClawSec is an encrypted netcat alternative for secure tunnels without
  certificates: data streams, file transfer, port forwarding, SOCKS5 and a TUN
  VPN, protected by a SPAKE2 password-authenticated key exchange (RFC 9382),
  AES-256-GCM and optional post-quantum ML-KEM-768.
authors:
  - family-names: Aleinikov
    given-names: Aleksei
    email: contact@alekseialeinikov.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/LF3551/ClawSec"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 4.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
keywords:
  - netcat
  - encryption
  - PAKE
  - SPAKE2
  - AES-GCM
  - post-quantum
  - ML-KEM
  - tunnel
  - VPN
